learnings:
  - The multi-agent-git collision is real and was happening live in this very session — the classroom agent's files churned the working tree throughout, which is exactly the pain Warpline targets
  - Warpline's conflict algebra (predict/consolidate/sem-delta) was already substrate-agnostic — only the store was git-coupled, so a native single-writer write path is a small, bounded addition, not a rewrite
  - stateId is a meaning-SET address (deduped) — never use it as a change-detector; the stableKey-keyed diff is the source of truth
  - 'Jinx''s false-AUTOFOLD risk is the gating correctness question for multi-writer: per-symbol structural essence can auto-fold cross-symbol semantic conflicts green (double-tax), and a primary auto-admitting store removes the human byte-diff that catches them'
