body: |-
  CONTEXT: User rejected the recovered "companion-first, not a frontal replacement" framing with the live pain: "multiple agents able to work using this new source control without being FUCKED by git. our system needs to NOT work with git and be its own thing." We were literally in the failure case — a second agent doing classroom work was bleeding ClassroomSection.tsx + routes/classroom.ts into our working tree throughout.

  TEAM (orchestrate plan→execute, then parallel Agent fan-out):
  - Arky (architect): the conflict algebra (predict/consolidate/sem-delta) is ALREADY substrate-agnostic; the store is the only git-coupled gap. Designed .warp/ object model, SCRATCH=O(1) pointer fork, consolidate-run-continuously as the multi-writer protocol, blobManifest for driftless export. Biggest unknown: symbol-domain CAS granularity.
  - Jinx (advocate): WARP≈Unison, PICK≈Pijul/Darcs, CAS≈Dolt/MVCC — the one novel thing is the TS checker-backed lens (needs none of the store rewrite). KILLER point: per-symbol structural essence is blind to cross-symbol semantic conflict (the double-tax 1.08×1.08 example) — as a primary auto-admitting store there's no human byte-diff backstop. The pain is the shared working tree, not git's object model. Proposed the false-AUTOFOLD adversarial corpus as the decisive cheap gate.
  - Loid (learning): multi-writer DEEPENS the moat via independent-convergence + graded-confidence-vs-outcome, IFF attribution is per-PICK (not per-WEFT) and calibration credits OUTCOME (not CAS-win). The one missing field = calibratedConfidence per PICK.

  RESOLUTION (user): "for this project we will continue to push and update git but we will be starting to manage and build out the ongoing history of this project's warpline." → coexistence. Build the native history NOW (single-writer), defer rip-out + multi-writer.

  BUILT: #strand (stateId=reproducible meaning address vs pickId=event identity w/ actor+time; reserved calibratedConfidence), #fabric (.warpline/fabric.jsonl + atomic refs/selvage), #pick (recordPick), WarpStore.loadState (disk read-back across CLI runs), gitUserName (read-only actor seed), CLI `pick`+`log`, $pick-flow, ~read-only extended to cover the write path (writes .warpline/ only, never git).

  BUG CAUGHT IN BUILD: no-op detection can't use stateId-equality — computeStateId hashes the DEDUPED essence set, so adding an identical-essence symbol leaves stateId unchanged while the meaning DID change. Fixed to diff-based detection + added a regression test.

  VERIFICATION: typecheck + build clean; 10 new fabric tests; full suite 123 green; genesis pick on this repo sealed 5162 objects (state:v0:2309baa8); .gitignore tracks the ledger, ignores heavy snapshots. Committed 7c9b1f63, pushed origin/warpline-surfaces.

  NEXT: (1) Jinx's false-AUTOFOLD gate — SHIP-GATE before any multi-writer auto-admission. (2) keep dogfooding picks; wire GUI Fabric to fabric.jsonl. Phase C (SCRATCH+per-domain CAS+WEFT) deferred until the gate passes.</parameter>
